A. Headline: median e_sym_gradient. Every reasonable variant of the
   three-point fit, so the reader can see the spread of answers.
==============================================================================
  d12 = five-seed median             slope -0.0240/depth  R2=0.181  NO CROSSING (trend is downward)
  d12 = five-seed min                slope +0.1618/depth  R2=0.511  crossing depth 46
  d12 = five-seed max                slope -0.1973/depth  R2=0.942  NO CROSSING (trend is downward)
  d12 = seed-7 only (seed-matched)   slope -0.1973/depth  R2=0.942  NO CROSSING (trend is downward)

  leave-one-out on the three depth points (d12 = five-seed median):
    drop d12: slope -0.1125/depth  NO CROSSING
    drop d14: slope -0.0240/depth  NO CROSSING
    drop d16: slope +0.0645/depth  crossing depth 87

  how big a change is even needed?
    d12 five-seed median            7.747e-07
    factor to reach 1e-4            129x
    observed d12->d16 change        -9.2%
    d12 seed sd-relative (I0001 stat) 56.7%
    I0001 detectability bar (2-3x sd) 113%-170%

==============================================================================
B. The three channels that DID move monotonically: how far is 1e-4?
==============================================================================

  e_sym_random: d12=8.274e-07 d14=1.274e-06 d16=1.870e-06  (2.26x over +4 depth)
    exponential in depth: slope +0.2038/depth R2=0.999 -> crossing depth 35
    power law in depth:   exponent +2.833 R2=1.000 -> crossing depth 65   (sqrt(depth) would be +0.500)

  e_lin_random: d12=7.666e-07 d14=7.751e-07 d16=8.717e-07  (1.14x over +4 depth)
    exponential in depth: slope +0.0321/depth R2=0.814 -> crossing depth 164
    power law in depth:   exponent +0.437 R2=0.780 -> crossing depth 865604   (sqrt(depth) would be +0.500)

  e_lin_update: d12=7.248e-07 d14=8.082e-07 d16=8.628e-07  (1.19x over +4 depth)
    exponential in depth: slope +0.0436/depth R2=0.980 -> crossing depth 125
    power law in depth:   exponent +0.608 R2=0.990 -> crossing depth 39211   (sqrt(depth) would be +0.500)

==============================================================================
C. Extrapolating the early transient (steps 1,2,3,5), exploratory
==============================================================================
  d12=1.193e-05 d14=8.282e-06 d16=1.006e-04
  d16 is already OVER 1e-4 here, and d14 is BELOW d12: the sequence
  is not monotone, so a crossing depth is not defined by a fit.
  (for the record, the 3-point log-linear fit: slope +0.5331, R2=0.625, crossing depth 16.9)
  the two adjacent-pair slopes it averages are -0.182 and +1.249 per unit depth - opposite signs, 6.8x apart in magnitude.

==============================================================================
D. Seed-uncertainty envelope on the crossing depth
==============================================================================
d14 and d16 have ONE seed each, so their points carry an unmeasured
seed error. Take the d12 sd-relative of the same channel as a proxy,
perturb d14 and d16 by +/- that, and sweep d12 over its five seeds.
45 variants per channel.

  e_sym_gradient: d12 sd-relative=56.7%   18/45 variants cross at all
      crossing depth among those: min=32  median=58  max=224
  e_sym_random: d12 sd-relative=41.5%   42/45 variants cross at all
      crossing depth among those: min=23  median=33  max=508
  e_lin_random: d12 sd-relative= 1.4%   45/45 variants cross at all
      crossing depth among those: min=131  median=160  max=199
  e_lin_update: d12 sd-relative= 2.2%   45/45 variants cross at all
      crossing depth among those: min=106  median=131  max=182
